# Budget alerts active by default for PAYGO accounts

We are turning on budget alerts by default for eligible Pay-As-You-Go (PAYGO) accounts. If your account does not already have a budget alert configured, Cloudflare will automatically create one for you with a $10 account-level threshold. 

This automatic alert will activate at the start of your next billing cycle, ensuring it does not trigger based on usage you have already incurred in your current cycle. 

## Why this matters

Usage-based products offer immense flexibility, but unexpected traffic spikes or testing environments can lead to billing surprises. By introducing a default threshold, Cloudflare provides immediate, proactive visibility into your account-level spending without requiring manual configuration. 

The default alert behaves exactly like a custom alert:
* **Informational only:** When your projected monthly usage-based spend reaches the $10 threshold, Cloudflare sends an email notification to the account administrators.
* **No service disruption:** This alert does not cap, throttle, or stop your active Cloudflare services or usage.

## Managing your alerts

You retain full control over your budget configurations. You can adjust the $10 threshold, set up additional tiered alerts, or opt out by removing the alert entirely. These adjustments can be made directly in the dashboard under **Manage Account** > **Billing** > **Billable Usage**, or via your account **Notifications** settings.

If you have already configured one or more custom budget alerts for your account, your settings will remain untouched and no default alert will be added. 

> **Note:** Default alerts apply strictly to PAYGO self-serve accounts utilizing active usage-based products. Enterprise contract accounts are not in scope for this update.

